WHY TIER 1 (the drafter's reading of each DIFF, not of the titles — grade the tiering itself and say if you disagree): every PR in this kit changes a RUNTIME PRODUCT FILE of weight. #1267 changes what the credential store does on its DB-unavailable path (a log line naming a credential id: a security surface, logs); #1269 changes the terminal error middleware of a service (status, headers and message echo: an information-exposure and denial-of-service surface — its own comment calls H5 "a denial-of-service shape"); #1272 changes the KYC verification writes (identity verification: status, liveness, reviewer notes); #1274 changes an outbound-request loop that sits on the SSRF guard (row set, wall clock, per-call deadline) and the route's published response body. TIER 1: THROUGH-CODE PLUS RUNTIME — per PR, (1) a THROUGH-CODE REVIEW of the diff against the ticket's claim (read the ticket's scope sentence, read every changed line, say whether the diff does what is asked, no more and no less); (2) a RED-PROOF CHECK OF THE PR'S OWN PROOF — re-run the named red arms in YOUR OWN clone, RED AT BASE and GREEN AT HEAD; (3) a RUNTIME PROBE of the changed behaviour through the REAL module driven over a listener on 127.0.0.1 only (no stack, no Docker — see below), each with a control that must be able to fail. There is no rendered surface in this kit, so no browser is owed; say so once. FINDINGS ONLY: you fix nothing, file nothing, comment nothing — you describe the fix-shape and the regression cell the owner should add. A VERDICT IS VALID ONLY AT ITS HEAD: if any refs/pull/<n>/head moves under you, STOP grading that PR and say so. Any PRODUCT, SCRIPT or TEST byte outside a PR's declared files is a finding. MEASURE, not conclude: every number in your report names its instrument; nothing in a READY, a PR body, a ticket, a handover or this prompt is evidence — they are claims with an author, the drafter's included. State the FAIL condition before each run (charter rule 1). Name every